  "description": "Make way for the north of England and hurry through the quaint commuter hills of Yorkshire; the complex Airedale & Wharfedale Network is ready for steadfast service in Train Sim World 7! Aboard modern Northern traction, operate across a variety of lines that converge into two major cities: Leeds and Bradford.\n\nToday’s network started in 1846 with the Leeds and Bradford Railway linking the two historic cities, and extending through the industrious hills to Skipton the following year, forming what is now known as the Airedale Line. The Midland Railway and the North Eastern co-owned the 1860s-built line to Ilkley, which would eventually form part of the Wharfedale Line. They have come a long way since, with the combined network being one of the busiest outside of the South East."
